<title>USA: Cali Realty acquisition accretive to EPS.</title>
<headline>Cali Realty acquisition accretive to EPS.</headline>
<dateline>CRANFORD, N.J. 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cali Realty Corp said on Monday its acquisition of Harborside Financial Center, a 1.9 million square foot office complex in Jersey City, is &quot;accretive to earnings.&quot;</p>
<p>Barry Lefkowitz, the company's chief financial officer said the deal gives Cali solid long-term financing and increases Cali's total portfolio by about 40 percent to 6.4 million square feet.</p>
<p>The company announced on September 30 it would pay $282.4 million for the office complex.</p>
</text>
